sue description**\nAfter updating to Godot Android Editor 4.7.1 Stable, the application takes an unusually long time to start.\n\nEvery time I launch the editor, it stays on the Android splash screen for about **2 minutes** before the Godot logo finally appears. In previous versions, startup was much faster.\n\nThe issue occurs before the editor interface is displayed, so no project needs to be opened.\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n\n1. Install and open Godot Android Editor 4.7.1 Stable.\n2. Wait for the application to start.\n3. The app remains on the Android splash screen for approximately **2 minutes** before continuing to the Godot logo.\n\n**Expected result**\nThe Godot logo should appear within a few seconds after the Android splash screen, as it did in previous versions.\n\n**Actual result**\nThe application remains on the Android splash screen for approximately **2 minutes** before the Godot logo appears and the editor finally opens.\n\n**Reproducibility**\nAlways (100%).\n\n**Additional information**\n\n* This issue only occurs in **Godot Android Editor 4.7.1 Stable**.\n* Previous versions (such as **4.7 Stable**) started normally and much faster on the same device.\n* No project needs to be opened for the issue to occur.\n* The issue happens before the editor UI is displayed.\n* I have not observed crashes; the application eventually opens after waiting.\n*\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n\n1. Install and open Godot Android Editor 4.7.1 Stable.\n2. Wait for the application to start.\n3. The app remains on the Android splash screen for approximately **fastest 22 minutes** before continuing to the Godot logo.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo project required ","closed_by":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.